# pdxwatch — caps.decl
#
# Wave: R102 userland graphical stack -- reference apps
# Milestone: M1 (scaffold + sys_taskinfo aggregation collectors)
# Doc:  paideia-os/paideia-os monorepo -- design/graphics/r102-user-plan.md
#       §2.8 (system-monitor GUI: role + data source + widget layout) and
#       §4.8 (per-issue landing plan for R102.M1..M5).
#
# pdxwatch is the R102 system-monitor GUI: the graphical peer of
# postui-top. It samples live-system stats once per second and renders
# them as three stacked widgets (CPU bar-per-core, memory tri-color,
# network sparkline) into a 480x360 KIND_SURFACE the compositor
# scans out.
#
# This M1-001 landing (Track C v1.1-A -- pdxwatch #11) retires the
# never-committed M1-001 STUB body: no scaffold code ever landed here,
# so v1.1-A skips the "seed a returns-0 stub" step entirely and lands
# the real syscall path directly. The v1.1 pass across the twelve
# mature R102/R100 satellites uses the same "leapfrog the stub"
# shape (postui-top #1 landed the equivalent real body in one round;
# pdxwatch mirrors it for the system-monitor role).
#
# The M1-001 real body compiles into two loose ELF64 objects
# (build-out/collectors.o + build-out/main.o) via tools/build.sh; the
# downstream link into build-out/pdxwatch (with a real _start binder)
# is a M1-002 packaging step, and the compositor / event-input wiring
# is M2/M3 material. Every M1-001 syscall goes through a thin
# `pw_sys_*` wrapper in src/collectors.pdx.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# KIND_SURFACE -- the render substrate (design/graphics/r102-user-
# plan.md §2.6 libpdx-gfx surface substrate)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# pdxwatch holds one KIND_SURFACE cap: a 480x360 BGRA8888 back-buffer
# minted at Main::main startup and committed once per second (or per
# damage-rect batch) via libpdx-gfx's gfx_commit into svc-compositor.
#
# Rights layout (mirror libpdx-gfx's SurfaceHandle rights table --
# design/graphics/r102-user-plan.md §7.2.1):
#
#   R_SURFACE_COMMIT   0x002   diff + commit a frame (the write analogue)
#   R_SURFACE_MINT     0x200   derive a surface from a KIND_MEMORY parent
#   R_SURFACE_REVOKE   0x020   teardown the surface row
#
# At M1-001 pdxwatch's collectors module (src/collectors.pdx) does
# NOT touch the surface -- the sys_taskinfo aggregation runs before
# any render. The mint + commit rights are declared HERE so the
# M1-002 window-creation landing (which introduces the surface_open
# + gfx_commit calls through libpdx-gfx) does not need a caps.decl
# churn.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT (subscribe) -- libpdx-event compositor channel
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# pdxwatch subscribes via libpdx-event.M3 to a compositor-emitted
# input channel; on POINTER_BUTTON_DOWN inside a CPU-bar rect the
# clicked bar cycles compact <-> expanded, on KEYDOWN 'q' the main
# loop exits. Declared here at M1-001 so the M3-001 input landing
# (which introduces event_next + event_poll) does not need to
# widen the manifest. Not exercised by the M1-001 collectors path
# (which is stat-side only).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# KIND_MEMORY -- the surface backing store + collector scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# KIND_SURFACE derives over KIND_MEMORY (= KIND_PAGE, 4). pdxwatch
# mints a KIND_MEMORY region sized 480 * 360 * 4 = 691_200 bytes at
# M1-002 startup and hands it to libpdx-gfx's surface_open, which
# performs the sys_cap_derive(KIND_SURFACE, ...) call; the derived
# surface cap is what libpdx-gfx subsequently invokes for every
# gfx_commit. The KIND_MEMORY authority is not held beyond the
# derive.
#
# The M1-001 collectors path itself does not mint memory -- its
# scratch (_pw_scratch, 64B taskinfo record staging) lives in .bss
# via `pub let mut ... : [u8; 64] = uninit @align(8)`, which the
# loader sizes as part of the ELF image.
#
requires:
- KIND_SURFACE(mint, commit, revoke)
- KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT(subscribe)
- KIND_MEMORY(mint, revoke)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Syscall dependencies (informational; not consumed by the InitCap
# sidecar -- the syscall gate is a kernel-side dispatch decision, not
# a per-process cap check at M1). Enumerated here so downstream
# tooling (release lint, dependency-audit) can trace pdxwatch's SC+
# surface without reading every .pdx source.
#
# The M1-001 collectors path uses exactly two syscalls (the peer
# postui-top uses the identical pair for the same reason: no
# CPU/memory/network-specific SC+ surface exists yet, so the poll
# module derives per-CPU active-task counts + total resident bytes
# from the same task_pool snapshot postui-top consumes):
#
#   * sysno 66  -- sys_clock_read_ns() -> u64 ns
#                  Monotonic ns-since-boot counter. collect_tick uses
#                  it to gate the fixed-interval refresh (converting
#                  the interval_ticks arg to a compatible ns-domain
#                  deadline via shift, per src/collectors.pdx §Tick
#                  semantics -- same 2^24-ns = 16.7ms tick as postui-
#                  top's poll module).
#   * sysno 83  -- sys_taskinfo(idx, user_buf_va)
#                             -> 0 | -ENOENT | -ESRCH | -EFAULT
#                  Ring-3 task-table introspection (paideia-os
#                  design/user/syscall-table.md row 83). Fills a 64-
#                  byte record per live task; collect_tick iterates
#                  idx = 0..PW_MAX_TASKS and derives:
#                    - task_state_counts[NEW..EXITED]  (from state
#                      field)
#                    - total_cpu_ticks  (sum of cpu_ticks field)
#                    - total_rss_pages  (sum of rss_pages field; 0
#                      at paideia-os HEAD pending PML4-walker
#                      landing -- see task_info.pdx §rss_pages)
#                    - per_cpu_active[0..PW_MAX_CPUS]  (naive
#                      round-robin bucketing until sys_cpuinfo /
#                      per-CPU affinity land in a follow-on round)
#
# The M2 render path will add libpdx-gfx's cap-invoke pathway (no
# extra sysno beyond the KIND_SURFACE R_SURFACE_COMMIT invocation);
# the M3 input path will add libpdx-event's sys_ipc_recv (sysno 40).
#
# v1.1-B (pdxwatch #12, LANDED) added the SysStatRecord@0.1 producer
# path through sys_semantic_send (sysno 115). Kernel body at
# paideia-os/src/kernel/core/syscall/handlers/sys_semantic_send.pdx
# (R107-M0-001 landing, paideia-os #2350; live at HEAD -- the
# dispatch table routes sysno 115 to sys_semantic_send_body). The
# userspace emit call lives in collect_tick's Phase D-bis (see
# src/collectors.pdx §V1.1-B "SEMANTIC-PIPE EMIT WIRE" LANDING).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
syscalls:
- sys_clock_read_ns @ 66
- sys_taskinfo      @ 83
- sys_semantic_send @ 115

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Declared output schemas
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# pdxwatch emits one first-class semantic-pipe schema at v1.1-B
# (pdxwatch #12, LANDED):
#
#   * SysStatRecord@0.1 -- one record per successful collect_tick
#                          refresh. Wire shape is a byte-for-byte
#                          prefix of the CollectSnapshot struct
#                          starting at CollectSnapshot[+32]:
#
#                            [+0 .. +64)   per_cpu_active[0..8]    (u64 x 8)
#                            [+64.. +72)   total_cpu_ticks         (u64)
#                            [+72.. +80)   total_rss_kb            (u64)
#                            [+80..+144)   task_state_counts[0..8] (u64 x 8)
#                            [+144..+152)  task_seen               (u64)
#                            [+152..+160)  task_skipped            (u64)
#
#                          = 160 bytes total, comfortably under the
#                          kernel's SSS_MAX_RECORD (240) cap with 80
#                          bytes headroom for a v0.2 tail extension
#                          (network sparkline stats, per-widget
#                          dirty telemetry). num_cpus is NOT
#                          emitted: the v1.1-A CollectSnapshot
#                          hard-codes num_cpus=1 at M1-001 and the
#                          per_cpu_active[8] slice already carries
#                          the CPU distribution; a future v0.2 that
#                          widens num_cpus emits it in the tail
#                          extension rather than repacking.
#
#                          Emitted through sys_semantic_send
#                          (sysno 115) with schema tag
#                          0x41545353 ('SSTA' little-endian, per
#                          the postui 4-char ASCII convention --
#                          transitional until libpdx-semantic-pipe's
#                          BLAKE3-hash schema registry lands).
#                          Every downstream scraper (e.g. a
#                          monitoring daemon reading
#                          `sysstat | pipe-consumer`) filters on
#                          this constant.
#
# The v1.1-A landing populated the in-memory snapshot only; v1.1-B
# (pdxwatch #12) adds the emit call in collect_tick's Phase D-bis.
# The emit is best-effort: sys_semantic_send failures increment a
# cumulative counter in the CollectSnapshot reserved region
# ([+192] emit_ok, [+200] emit_fail) so a witness can assert the
# collector's emit path is running without a KIND_SEMANTIC_PIPE
# consumer wired up, and the tick still commits regardless (a
# transient emit fault does not de-sync the stats-side aggregate).
declares_output_schemas:
- SysStatRecord@0.1
